"""Printed 165 Exercise 6.3; exact decompositions independently multiplied back."""
from math12_reviewed_unit1 import heading,paragraph,page
QUESTIONS=[
 r'Evaluate after partial fractions: (a) \(\int\frac1{x(x-3)}\,dx\); (b) \(\int\frac{3x^2+2x-1}{x(x+1)}\,dx\); (c) \(\int\frac{4x^3+4x^2+x-1}{x^2(x+1)^2}\,dx\); (d) \(\int\frac1{x^3-1}\,dx\); (e) \(\int\frac{x^4-x^2+2}{x^2(x-1)}\,dx\); (f) \(\int\frac1{x^2-1}\,dx\); (g) \(\int\frac{x-3}{2x^2-x-1}\,dx\); (h) \(\int\frac{x^2-1}{x^2-2x-15}\,dx\); (i) \(\int\frac{x}{(x+1)(x^2+1)}\,dx\); (j) \(\int\frac{x^2+2}{(x^2+1)^2}\,dx\).',
 r'The rate at which the body eliminates a drug (in milliliters per hour) is given by \(R(t)/dt=60t/[(t+1)^2(t+2)]\), where t is the number of hours since the drug was administered. If R(0) = 0 is the current drug elimination, how much of the drug is eliminated during the first hour after it was administered? The fourth hour, after it was administered?',
 r'The rate of change of the voting population of a city with respect to time t (in years) is estimated to be \(dN/dt=100t/(1+t^2)^2\), where N(t) is in thousands. If N(0) is the current voting population, then how much will this population increase during the next 3 years?',
 r'An oil tanker aground on a reef is losing oil and producing an oil slick that is radiating outward at a rate approximated by \(dr/dt=100/\sqrt{t^2+9}\), t ≥ 0. where r is the radius (in feet) of the circular slick after t minutes. Find the radius of the slick after 4 minutes if the radius is r = 0 when t = 0.'
]
STEPS=[
 ['Perform long division when needed; include all repeated factor powers and preserve exclusions from the original denominator.', '(a) 1/[x(x−3)] = −1/(3x)+1/[3(x−3)]. Integrate: (1/3)ln|(x−3)/x|+C, x ≠ 0,3.', '(b) Division and decomposition give 3−1/x+0/(x+1). Integrate: 3x−ln|x|+C. The original expression still excludes x = 0 and −1, despite cancellation of x+1.', '(c) The decomposition is 3/x−1/x²+1/(x+1)−2/(x+1)². Integrate: 3ln|x|+1/x+ln|x+1|+2/(x+1)+C, excluding 0,−1.', '(d) Factor x³−1 = (x−1)(x²+x+1). The decomposition is 1/[3(x−1)]−(x+2)/[3(x²+x+1)].', 'Write the quadratic numerator as −(2x+1)/6−1/2. Integrate to (1/3)ln|x−1|−(1/6)ln(x²+x+1)−(1/√3)arctan((2x+1)/√3)+C, x ≠ 1.', '(e) Long division gives x+1, and the remaining decomposition is −2/x−2/x²+2/(x−1). Integrate: x²/2+x−2ln|x|+2/x+2ln|x−1|+C, excluding 0,1.', '(f) 1/(x²−1) = 1/[2(x−1)]−1/[2(x+1)]. Integrate: (1/2)ln|(x−1)/(x+1)|+C, excluding ±1.', '(g) Factor 2x²−x−1 = (x−1)(2x+1). Decompose as −2/[3(x−1)]+7/[3(2x+1)]. Integrate: −(2/3)ln|x−1|+(7/6)ln|2x+1|+C, excluding 1,−1/2.', '(h) Division gives 1+3/(x−5)−1/(x+3). Integrate: x+3ln|x−5|−ln|x+3|+C, excluding 5,−3.', '(i) Decompose as −1/[2(x+1)]+(x+1)/[2(x²+1)]. Integrate: −(1/2)ln|x+1|+(1/4)ln(x²+1)+(1/2)arctan x+C, x ≠ −1.', '(j) (x²+2)/(x²+1)² = 1/(x²+1)+1/(x²+1)². Integrate: (3/2)arctan x+x/[2(x²+1)]+C for all real x.', 'Each decomposition was checked by clearing its denominator and comparing every polynomial coefficient; differentiating the integrated terms reproduces the original rational function on its domain.'],
 ['Interpret the printed rate R(t)/dt as dR/dt; as written it is not derivative notation. Let R be cumulative millilitres eliminated and t ≥ 0.', 'Decompose 60t/[(t+1)²(t+2)] = 120/(t+1)−60/(t+1)²−120/(t+2).', 'Integrate: R(t) = 120ln(t+1)+60/(t+1)−120ln(t+2)+C.', 'Use R(0) = 0: 60−120ln 2+C = 0, so C = 120ln 2−60.', 'The first hour is the interval [0,1]: R(1)−R(0) = 120ln(4/3)−30 ≈ 4.521848694 ml.', 'The fourth hour is [3,4], not [0,4]. It eliminates R(4)−R(3) = 120ln(25/24)−3 ≈ 1.898639342 ml.', 'Both quantities are positive because the rate is nonnegative for t ≥ 0; report approximately 4.52 ml and 1.90 ml.'],
 ['The requested increase is N(3)−N(0) = ∫₀³100t/(1+t²)² dt, measured in thousands.', 'Set u = 1+t², du = 2t dt.', 'Then the antiderivative is 50∫u⁻² du = −50/u+C = −50/(1+t²)+C.', 'At 3, this is −5+C; at 0, it is −50+C.', 'Subtract: N(3)−N(0) = 45 thousands.', 'Thus the voting population increases by 45,000 people, independent of its current absolute size.', 'The rate is positive for t > 0, so the sign and unit conversion agree with the model.'],
 ['Integrate the radial growth rate from 0 to 4 minutes: r(4) = ∫₀⁴100/√(t²+9) dt.', 'A primitive is 100ln(t+√(t²+9))+C.', 'Enforce r(0) = 0: the logarithm at 0 is ln 3, so C = −100ln 3.', 'Therefore r(t) = 100ln[(t+√(t²+9))/3], t ≥ 0.', 'At 4, √(16+9) = 5 and the logarithm argument is (4+5)/3 = 3.', 'Hence r(4) = 100ln 3 ≈ 109.861228867 feet, or 109.86 feet.', 'This is a radius, not an area. The equivalent formula 100asinh(t/3) has derivative 100/√(t²+9) and starts at zero.']
]
ANSWERS=['(a) (1/3)ln|(x−3)/x|+C; (b) 3x−ln|x|+C; (c) 3ln|x|+ln|x+1|+1/x+2/(x+1)+C; (d) (1/3)ln|x−1|−(1/6)ln(x²+x+1)−arctan((2x+1)/√3)/√3+C; (e) x²/2+x−2ln|x|+2/x+2ln|x−1|+C; (f) (1/2)ln|(x−1)/(x+1)|+C; (g) −(2/3)ln|x−1|+(7/6)ln|2x+1|+C; (h) x+3ln|x−5|−ln|x+3|+C; (i) −(1/2)ln|x+1|+(1/4)ln(x²+1)+(1/2)arctan x+C; (j) (3/2)arctan x+x/[2(x²+1)]+C.', 'First hour: 120ln(4/3)−30 ≈ 4.52 ml. Fourth hour: 120ln(25/24)−3 ≈ 1.90 ml.', '45,000 people.', '100ln 3 ≈ 109.86 feet.']
PAGES=[page('087_page_1.jpg',165,[heading('Exercise 6.3')]+[paragraph(str(i+1)+'. '+q) for i,q in enumerate(QUESTIONS)])]
